From 343820deff0cd7296e48487126aaa7c87824a1f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 03:44:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(assignments): stop resubmissions destroying the
 previous attempt

AssignmentService::submit() used updateOrCreate keyed on (assignment, student),
so a second submission overwrote the first in place. Two consequences:

- The earlier text, file, timestamp and late flag were lost with no history
  and nothing in the audit trail recording what was replaced.
- Grade fields were NOT reset, so an instructor's score stayed attached to
  content they had never seen. A student could resubmit after grading and
  keep the mark.

The unique (assignment_id, student_id) index is left intact; the current row
stays canonical and prior states are archived additively into a new
assignment_submission_versions table. Resubmitting now bumps attempt_no,
snapshots the previous attempt with its grade, and clears the stale grade so
the work is re-marked. Assignments gain allow_resubmission (default true,
preserving today's behaviour) and refuse a second submission when it is off.

Audit records resubmissions as assignments.resubmit, distinct from the
first submission.

Adds AssignmentResubmissionIntegrityTest; all four cases fail on the previous
behaviour.
